1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,920
The Porsche nine eighteen Spyder hides two

2
00:00:02,920 --> 00:00:05,424
secrets that you cannot see from the

3
00:00:05,424 --> 00:00:07,163
outside, and one you can.

4
00:00:07,343 --> 00:00:09,613
The exhaust pipes come out of the

5
00:00:09,613 --> 00:00:10,644
top of the car,

6
00:00:10,644 --> 00:00:11,814
above the engine,

7
00:00:11,814 --> 00:00:14,840
and Porsche says no other production vehicle

8
00:00:14,840 --> 00:00:15,528
does that.

9
00:00:15,708 --> 00:00:17,612
The rear wheels steer.

10
00:00:17,792 --> 00:00:20,306
And a button on the steering wheel

11
00:00:20,306 --> 00:00:23,264
called Hot Lap spends the battery's last

12
00:00:23,264 --> 00:00:25,408
reserves for a few fast laps.

13
00:00:25,588 --> 00:00:26,860
These are the facts,

14
00:00:26,860 --> 00:00:28,514
with every figure sourced.

15
00:00:28,863 --> 00:00:32,500
We use Porsche's own twenty thirteen press

16
00:00:32,500 --> 00:00:35,097
release as published by 911uk,

17
00:00:35,097 --> 00:00:38,386
a March twenty twelve report from Auto

18
00:00:38,386 --> 00:00:39,598
one two three,

19
00:00:39,598 --> 00:00:43,235
and Wikipedia, Car and Driver's figures as

20
00:00:43,235 --> 00:00:44,793
quoted there, evo,

21
00:00:44,793 --> 00:00:46,871
and the duPont Registry.

22
00:00:47,051 --> 00:00:50,522
Where Porsche's own figures changed over time,

23
00:00:50,522 --> 00:00:51,428
we show how.

24
00:00:51,608 --> 00:00:53,417
Where sources disagree,

25
00:00:53,417 --> 00:00:54,440
we show both.

26
00:00:54,620 --> 00:00:56,650
And all arithmetic is ours,

27
00:00:56,650 --> 00:00:57,627
and labelled.

28
00:00:57,978 --> 00:00:58,906
Secret one.

29
00:00:59,086 --> 00:01:02,057
Porsche's press release says the exhaust has

30
00:01:02,057 --> 00:01:03,677
what it calls top pipes,

31
00:01:03,677 --> 00:01:05,973
ending in the upper rear body just

32
00:01:05,973 --> 00:01:07,120
above the engine.

33
00:01:07,300 --> 00:01:10,062
The release says this layout reduces back

34
00:01:10,062 --> 00:01:12,824
pressure and keeps the engine bay cooler,

35
00:01:12,824 --> 00:01:14,441
which helps the battery.

36
00:01:14,621 --> 00:01:17,630
And Porsche states that no other production

37
00:01:17,630 --> 00:01:19,520
vehicle uses this solution.

38
00:01:19,700 --> 00:01:21,320
That is Porsche's claim,

39
00:01:21,320 --> 00:01:23,144
not an independent finding,

40
00:01:23,144 --> 00:01:24,832
but it is a striking one.

41
00:01:25,181 --> 00:01:27,952
The March twenty twelve report from Auto

42
00:01:27,952 --> 00:01:30,723
one two three describes the same feature

43
00:01:30,723 --> 00:01:33,355
as an upward-venting top pipes system.

44
00:01:33,535 --> 00:01:35,168
So it was in the car from

45
00:01:35,168 --> 00:01:36,278
the early stages,

46
00:01:36,278 --> 00:01:38,237
and not a late styling choice.

47
00:01:38,417 --> 00:01:40,574
The reason the exhaust matters is the

48
00:01:40,574 --> 00:01:41,041
battery.

49
00:01:41,221 --> 00:01:43,763
A lithium-ion pack works best in a

50
00:01:43,763 --> 00:01:45,707
narrow temperature window,

51
00:01:45,707 --> 00:01:48,848
and Porsche says optimum performance is at

52
00:01:48,848 --> 00:01:51,240
twenty to forty degrees Celsius.

53
00:01:51,590 --> 00:01:52,830
By our arithmetic,

54
00:01:52,830 --> 00:01:55,448
a twenty-degree window is a narrow one

55
00:01:55,448 --> 00:01:57,445
for a car that can make eight

56
00:01:57,445 --> 00:02:01,027
hundred eighty-seven metric horsepower in the engine

57
00:02:01,027 --> 00:02:02,887
bay of a mid-engined coupé.

58
00:02:03,067 --> 00:02:05,631
The press release says the battery is

59
00:02:05,631 --> 00:02:08,957
liquid-cooled and has three hundred twelve cells

60
00:02:08,957 --> 00:02:11,798
and about seven kilowatt-hours of energy.

61
00:02:11,978 --> 00:02:14,256
Moving the exhaust to the top frees

62
00:02:14,256 --> 00:02:16,275
the engine bay from some of the

63
00:02:16,275 --> 00:02:18,619
heat, and that is the stated reason.

64
00:02:18,968 --> 00:02:21,067
The engine behind the pipes has a

65
00:02:21,067 --> 00:02:21,639
pedigree.

66
00:02:21,819 --> 00:02:25,496
Porsche's release says the four point six

67
00:02:25,496 --> 00:02:28,277
litre V8 is derived from the RS

68
00:02:28,277 --> 00:02:30,878
Spyder race car's power unit,

69
00:02:30,878 --> 00:02:34,017
makes six hundred eight horsepower,

70
00:02:34,017 --> 00:02:36,888
and can run to nine thousand one

71
00:02:36,888 --> 00:02:38,502
hundred fifty rpm.

72
00:02:38,682 --> 00:02:40,961
It adds that the output of about

73
00:02:40,961 --> 00:02:44,237
one hundred thirty-two horsepower per litre is

74
00:02:44,237 --> 00:02:47,513
the highest of any naturally aspirated Porsche

75
00:02:47,513 --> 00:02:50,646
engine, against the Carrera GT's one hundred

76
00:02:50,646 --> 00:02:50,931
six.

77
00:02:51,280 --> 00:02:52,604
Check that arithmetic.

78
00:02:52,784 --> 00:02:56,138
Six hundred eight horsepower divided by four

79
00:02:56,138 --> 00:02:58,959
point five nine three litres is about

80
00:02:58,959 --> 00:03:00,713
one hundred thirty-two,

81
00:03:00,713 --> 00:03:03,686
so Porsche's per-litre number is right.

82
00:03:03,866 --> 00:03:05,148
By our arithmetic,

83
00:03:05,148 --> 00:03:08,209
that is twenty-four percent better than the

84
00:03:08,209 --> 00:03:10,275
Carrera GT's one hundred six.

85
00:03:10,455 --> 00:03:13,889
Wikipedia lists the same engine's peak power

86
00:03:13,889 --> 00:03:16,075
at eighty-seven hundred rpm,

87
00:03:16,075 --> 00:03:18,886
which is below the nine thousand one

88
00:03:18,886 --> 00:03:22,789
hundred fifty maximum engine speed Porsche quotes,

89
00:03:22,789 --> 00:03:26,302
so the two numbers describe different things.

90
00:03:26,653 --> 00:03:29,218
More engine details from the release.

91
00:03:29,398 --> 00:03:33,243
Dry-sump lubrication and carbon fibre parts,

92
00:03:33,243 --> 00:03:35,253
including the oil tank,

93
00:03:35,253 --> 00:03:38,137
air filter box and air induction,

94
00:03:38,137 --> 00:03:39,186
save weight.

95
00:03:39,366 --> 00:03:42,140
Titanium connecting rods are used.

96
00:03:42,320 --> 00:03:45,790
The seven-speed PDK gearbox is rotated one

97
00:03:45,790 --> 00:03:49,260
hundred eighty degrees to lower the centre

98
00:03:49,260 --> 00:03:50,169
of gravity.

99
00:03:50,349 --> 00:03:52,421
So the pipes are only one of

100
00:03:52,421 --> 00:03:55,529
several unusual choices in the engine bay,

101
00:03:55,529 --> 00:03:58,119
and each is described by Porsche as

102
00:03:58,119 --> 00:04:00,043
a weight or heat decision.

103
00:04:00,393 --> 00:04:02,529
Secret two is at the other end.

104
00:04:02,709 --> 00:04:05,973
Porsche's release says each rear wheel steers

105
00:04:05,973 --> 00:04:08,874
up to three degrees in either direction.

106
00:04:09,054 --> 00:04:11,341
At low speeds the rear wheels turn

107
00:04:11,341 --> 00:04:12,687
opposite the fronts,

108
00:04:12,687 --> 00:04:14,975
which tightens the turning circle.

109
00:04:15,155 --> 00:04:17,430
At higher speeds they turn in the

110
00:04:17,430 --> 00:04:19,429
same direction as the fronts,

111
00:04:19,429 --> 00:04:22,945
which improves stability during quick lane changes.

112
00:04:23,125 --> 00:04:24,532
By our arithmetic,

113
00:04:24,532 --> 00:04:26,956
three degrees is a small angle,

114
00:04:26,956 --> 00:04:29,380
but at the rear axle it changes

115
00:04:29,380 --> 00:04:30,788
how the car turns.

116
00:04:31,138 --> 00:04:33,623
The Auto one two three report from

117
00:04:33,623 --> 00:04:37,059
March twenty twelve calls it adaptive real-axle

118
00:04:37,059 --> 00:04:39,764
steering, which looks like a typo for

119
00:04:39,764 --> 00:04:40,495
rear-axle.

120
00:04:40,675 --> 00:04:43,113
We mention the typo because it shows

121
00:04:43,113 --> 00:04:45,551
how early the feature was announced.

122
00:04:45,731 --> 00:04:47,862
The sources do not give the speed

123
00:04:47,862 --> 00:04:50,187
at which the rear wheels change from

124
00:04:50,187 --> 00:04:51,931
opposite to same direction.

125
00:04:52,111 --> 00:04:54,117
So we can describe the principle,

126
00:04:54,117 --> 00:04:55,455
but not the threshold.

127
00:04:55,804 --> 00:04:58,314
The car is also adaptive in its

128
00:04:58,314 --> 00:04:58,637
air.

129
00:04:58,817 --> 00:05:02,393
Porsche Active Aerodynamics has three modes,

130
00:05:02,393 --> 00:05:06,050
from maximum efficiency to maximum downforce.

131
00:05:06,230 --> 00:05:07,201
In Race mode,

132
00:05:07,201 --> 00:05:09,813
Porsche says, the rear wing sits at

133
00:05:09,813 --> 00:05:10,858
a steep angle,

134
00:05:10,858 --> 00:05:12,351
the spoiler extends,

135
00:05:12,351 --> 00:05:15,487
and underfloor flaps open to create ground

136
00:05:15,487 --> 00:05:17,353
effect at the front axle.

137
00:05:17,533 --> 00:05:19,136
In the efficient modes,

138
00:05:19,136 --> 00:05:21,995
the air inlets under the headlights close

139
00:05:21,995 --> 00:05:24,785
after pull-away, and reopen at about one

140
00:05:24,785 --> 00:05:27,713
hundred thirty kilometres per hour or when

141
00:05:27,713 --> 00:05:29,178
cooling demand rises.

142
00:05:29,527 --> 00:05:30,874
Here is a conversion.

143
00:05:31,054 --> 00:05:34,245
One hundred thirty kilometres per hour is

144
00:05:34,245 --> 00:05:36,735
about eighty-one miles per hour,

145
00:05:36,735 --> 00:05:38,136
by our arithmetic.

146
00:05:38,316 --> 00:05:39,863
So below highway speed,

147
00:05:39,863 --> 00:05:42,418
the inlets are closed in the efficient

148
00:05:42,418 --> 00:05:44,435
modes, and above it they open.

149
00:05:44,615 --> 00:05:46,743
The car adapts its shape to the

150
00:05:46,743 --> 00:05:48,047
speed and the mode,

151
00:05:48,047 --> 00:05:50,930
which makes it a moving aerodynamic device

152
00:05:50,930 --> 00:05:52,440
and not a fixed shape.

153
00:05:52,789 --> 00:05:53,741
Now the button.

154
00:05:53,921 --> 00:05:56,859
Porsche's release says there are five drive

155
00:05:56,859 --> 00:05:59,113
modes selected by a map switch on

156
00:05:59,113 --> 00:06:00,411
the steering wheel.

157
00:06:00,591 --> 00:06:03,002
E-Power is the default when the battery

158
00:06:03,002 --> 00:06:04,486
is sufficiently charged,

159
00:06:04,486 --> 00:06:07,206
with the combustion engine running only when

160
00:06:07,206 --> 00:06:07,639
needed.

161
00:06:07,819 --> 00:06:10,141
Hybrid focuses on efficiency.

162
00:06:10,321 --> 00:06:13,199
Sport Hybrid keeps the engine running as

163
00:06:13,199 --> 00:06:14,350
the main source,

164
00:06:14,350 --> 00:06:15,789
with electric boost.

165
00:06:15,969 --> 00:06:18,407
Race Hybrid uses the engine for high

166
00:06:18,407 --> 00:06:20,439
loads and charges the battery.

167
00:06:20,619 --> 00:06:23,297
And Hot Lap is a button inside

168
00:06:23,297 --> 00:06:24,369
Race Hybrid.

169
00:06:24,718 --> 00:06:26,537
Hot Lap, Porsche says,

170
00:06:26,537 --> 00:06:29,761
pushes the battery to its maximum power

171
00:06:29,761 --> 00:06:32,241
output for a few fast laps and

172
00:06:32,241 --> 00:06:35,051
uses all available battery energy.

173
00:06:35,231 --> 00:06:36,822
That is the sentence.

174
00:06:37,002 --> 00:06:38,363
By our arithmetic,

175
00:06:38,363 --> 00:06:41,009
with a seven kilowatt-hour battery,

176
00:06:41,009 --> 00:06:43,580
there is not much energy to spend:

177
00:06:43,580 --> 00:06:46,378
a car using two hundred ten kilowatts

178
00:06:46,378 --> 00:06:50,159
of electric power would drain seven kilowatt-hours

179
00:06:50,159 --> 00:06:51,747
in about two minutes.

180
00:06:52,096 --> 00:06:53,919
We should be clear about that sum.

181
00:06:54,099 --> 00:06:56,609
It assumes the full two hundred ten

182
00:06:56,609 --> 00:06:59,190
kilowatts from both electric motors,

183
00:06:59,190 --> 00:07:01,700
one hundred fifteen at the rear and

184
00:07:01,700 --> 00:07:03,493
ninety-five at the front,

185
00:07:03,493 --> 00:07:04,855
as Wikipedia lists,

186
00:07:04,855 --> 00:07:07,365
and that all of the battery's seven

187
00:07:07,365 --> 00:07:09,157
kilowatt-hours is usable.

188
00:07:09,337 --> 00:07:11,926
Neither assumption is in our sources.

189
00:07:12,106 --> 00:07:14,272
It is only a sense of scale:

190
00:07:14,272 --> 00:07:16,361
the Hot Lap button is a few

191
00:07:16,361 --> 00:07:17,599
minutes of help,

192
00:07:17,599 --> 00:07:18,759
not a long one.

193
00:07:19,108 --> 00:07:22,037
Porsche's figures for the nine eighteen changed

194
00:07:22,037 --> 00:07:24,653
during development, and the sources let us

195
00:07:24,653 --> 00:07:25,401
follow them.

196
00:07:25,581 --> 00:07:27,034
In March twenty twelve,

197
00:07:27,034 --> 00:07:29,623
Auto one two three reports Porsche saying

198
00:07:29,623 --> 00:07:32,338
more than seven hundred seventy horsepower.

199
00:07:32,518 --> 00:07:34,874
By the twenty thirteen press release it

200
00:07:34,874 --> 00:07:36,686
